From: Phase14 audit <audit@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:41:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/20] fix(scope): bring Phase 14 back inside section M; og
 twins render in prebuild
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner instruction 2026-09-02 ("偏离项按照计划修正"): the items the Phase 14
report flagged as beyond the approved plan are reverted or completed as
planned.
- redirects: the five non-JP nfc-reader-writer rules return to the family hub
  /products/rfid-readers/ (only the JP rule was approved for the encoder
  page); the two translation-inferred LEGIC targets (IT carta-legale, FR
  carte-legendaire) go to the card family hub instead of the LEGIC SKU
- forms: the /faq/ Kadence form rewire and the contact <noscript> removal
  are dropped (enhance-page.ts back to baseline); the approved B5 scope —
  inline RFQ / sample-pack hardening and the dead homepage newsletter row —
  stands
- schema: /about/* pages no longer count as article routes (AboutPage only,
  as Phase 10 intended)
- og twins: scripts/build-og-rasters.mjs runs in prebuild — renders missing
  twins locally with sharp, runs --check on Vercel/CI — so the committed
  twins stay the deterministic source while new SVG heroes cannot ship
  without one
